activation	Print prompt	2026-10-27T09:48:45.8299038Z {"title": "Arrow scan of list<dictionary> fails when the first 2048 rows hold no list elements", "body": "### What happens?\n\nScanning an Arrow `list<dictionary<int32, string>>` column fails with an internal error when the first scan chunk (the first 2048 rows) contains zero list elements and later rows contain values:\n\n```\nINTERNAL Error: Attempted to dereference unique_ptr that is NULL!\n```\n\nIn DuckDB-WASM (1.31.0, DuckDB v1.4.0) the same input produces `Failed to cast ArrowTypeInfo, type mismatch (expected: STRING, got: LIST)`, and the database is then invalidated. That is how we hit it in production: `insertArrowFromIPCStream` into a `VARCHAR[]` table.\n\nIt passes when the child is plain `utf8`, and when even one of the first 2048 rows holds a value. It also passes when the only all-empty chunk is not the first one.\n\nThe cause appears to be the empty-list shortcut in `ArrowToDuckDBList` (`src/function/table/arrow_conversion.cpp#L228-L233` (upstream source reference)):\n\n```cpp\nif (list_size == 0 && start_offset == 0) {\n    D_ASSERT(!child_array.dictionary);\n    ArrowToDuckDBConversion::ColumnArrowToDuckDB(child_vector, child_array, chunk_offset, child_state, list_size,\n                                                 child_type, -1);\n    return;\n}\n```\n\n`start_offset == 0` with `list_size == 0` only happens when no earlier row had elements, so it is reached only by an empty first chunk. A dictionary-encoded child reaches it despite the debug-only assert, and it is converted as a plain column. For a dictionary child, `child_type` is the index type, which `arrow_duck_schema.cpp#L80-L81` (upstream source reference) builds as `ArrowType(INTEGER)` with no `type_info`. The `VARCHAR` branch then calls `arrow_type.GetTypeInfo<ArrowStringInfo>()` (`arrow_conversion.cpp#L846` (upstream source reference)) on that null `type_info`. The WASM build presumably doesn't trap the null read, which would explain its type-mismatch message instead of the null-dereference error.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport duckdb\nimport pyarrow as pa\n\n# 2049 rows: the first 2048 lists are empty, the last holds one value.\noffsets = pa.array([0] * 2049 + [1], pa.int32())\nchild = pa.array([\"a\"]).dictionary_encode()  # dictionary<values=string, indices=int32>\ntbl = pa.table({\"l\": pa.ListArray.from_arrays(offsets, child)})\n\nprint(duckdb.sql(\"SELECT * FROM tbl\").fetchall()[-1])\n```\n\nResult: `_duckdb.InternalException: INTERNAL Error: Attempted to dereference unique_ptr that is NULL!`\n\nExpected: `(['a'],)`, which is what you get after removing `.dictionary_encode()`.\n\n### OS:\n\nmacOS 27.0, arm64\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\n1.5.6 (also 1.4.0, and the same code is on `main` at 8681dc52)\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\nPython (pyarrow 25.0.1); also DuckDB-WASM 1.31.0\n\n### Hardware:\n\nApple Silicon\n\n### Full Name:\n\nOliver Kaisti\n\n### Affiliation:\n\nSitedrive\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nYes (the script generates its own data)\n"}
